      "summary": "A first-party Launch HN announcement describes a small event-dispatching core, ordered plugins and format-aware streams for AI routing and inspection.",
      "body": [
        "Respan introduced its open-source Rust AI gateway in a first-party Launch HN post on October 20. Rather than putting every provider and policy into the gateway core, the design exposes public interfaces for plugins. The announcement describes providers, protocols, routing, fallbacks and example privacy filters as extensions around a small event-dispatching core. The project is still pre-alpha, so its architecture should not be mistaken for a production-readiness guarantee.",
        "An adapter gives a connection to a client format, which represents requests and responses as typed streams. Plugins run in registration order and can select a provider, inspect or wrap streams, make additional calls, return a response or refuse a request. When client and provider formats match and no plugin changes the payload, original bytes and provider-specific fields can pass through unchanged; cross-format requests use shared representations for messages, tools and usage.",
        "For teams instrumenting agents, that makes plugin order and translation boundaries important places to test whether telemetry stays faithful. Respan distinguishes the self-hostable gateway from its commercial hosted platform, which adds native observability and evaluations. The announcement provides implementation details, not independent reliability or performance results."
